===Title roles===
====''Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice'' (2016)====
{{main|Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice |l1=''Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice''}}
[[File:Ben Affleck by Gage Skidmore.jpg|thumb|upright|Ben Affleck in 2015]]

Press speculation about a sequel to ''[[Man of Steel (film)|Man of Steel]]'' (2013) preceded the [[San Diego Comic-Con#Locations and dates|46th San Diego Comic-Con]].<ref>{{cite news|last=Sperling|first=Nicole|title=Comic-Con 2013: 'Superman & Batman' movie will follow 'Man of Steel'|url=http://herocomplex.latimes.com/movies/comic-con-2013-superman-batman-movie-will-follow-man-of-steel/#/0|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=July 20, 2013|access-date=December 29, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130721024848/http://herocomplex.latimes.com/movies/comic-con-2013-superman-batman-movie-will-follow-man-of-steel/#/0|archive-date=July 21, 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/superman-batman-film-set-comic-589521|title=Superman & Batman Film Set for Comic-Con Reveal|date=July 20, 2013|first=Borys|last=Kit|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|access-date=October 1, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251204164616/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/superman-batman-film-set-comic-589521/|archive-date=December 4, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> At that event, director [[Zack Snyder]] announced ''Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice'' as ''Man of Steel''{{'s}} follow-up, based on a narrative inspired by ''The Dark Knight Returns''.<ref>{{cite web|last=Anders|first=Charlie Jane|url=http://io9.com/theyre-doing-a-superman-batman-movie-but-thats-not-851711013|title=They're doing a Superman/Batman movie... but that's not the big news|work=[[io9]]|date=July 20, 2013|access-date=July 22, 2013|archive-date=July 22, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130722040226/http://io9.com/theyre-doing-a-superman-batman-movie-but-thats-not-851711013|url-status=dead}}</ref> Goyer returned to develop a screenplay that was rewritten at least three times, including once by [[Chris Terrio]], because he was working concurrently on other projects of the [[DC Extended Universe]] (DCEU).<ref name=sds>{{Cite web |url= https://www.setdecorators.org/?art=film_decor_features&SHOW=SetDecor_Film_BATMAN_V_SUPERMAN |title= Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice |last=Burg |first=Karen |date=May 9, 2016|publisher=Set Decorators Society of America|url-status=live |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20251229182052/https://www.setdecorators.org/?art=film_decor_features&SHOW=SetDecor_Film_BATMAN_V_SUPERMAN |archive-date=December 29, 2025 |access-date=December 29, 2025}}</ref><ref name="TerrioIn">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/batman-superman-chris-terrio-write-666735 |title=Batman-Superman Film Enlists 'Argo' Writer (Exclusive)|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|first= Tatiana |last= Siegel|date=December 18, 2013 |access-date=December 18, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250307171958/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/batman-superman-chris-terrio-write-666735/|archive-date=March 7, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Terrio's script was influenced by ''The Dark Knight'' films, philosopher [[Umberto Eco]]'s "The Myth of Superman" essay, and "Musée des Beaux Arts", an allegorical poem by English poet [[W. H. Auden]].<ref name="WSJ">{{cite web|url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-great-comic-book-movie-debate-1457637539|title=The Great Comic-Book Movie Debate|first=Ben|last=Fritz |date=March 10, 2016|work=[[The Wall Street Journal]]|access-date=February 23, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160402084921/https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-great-comic-book-movie-debate-1457637539|archive-date=April 2, 2016|url-status=live|url-access=subscription}}</ref>

Nolan worked as an executive producer, albeit in an advisory role, but Warner Bros. did not approach Bale to reprise Batman.<ref name="Abid">{{cite news|first= Abid |last= Rahman|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/news/ben-affleck-first-choice-batman-740292|title=Charles Roven: Ben Affleck "Was the First Guy We Went to" for Batman Role|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|date=October 13, 2014|access-date=October 13, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251126205138/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/ben-affleck-first-choice-batman-740292/|archive-date=November 26, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.esquire.co.uk/culture/film-tv/7424/christian-bale-interview/|title=Christian Bale Is Esquire's January Cover Star|date=December 10, 2014|first=Johnny|last=Davis|work=[[Esquire (magazine)|Esquire]]|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150710044125/http://www.esquire.co.uk/culture/film-tv/7424/christian-bale-interview/|archive-date=July 10, 2015|access-date=December 29, 2025}}</ref> [[Ben Affleck]] stars in [[Bruce Wayne (DC Extended Universe)|said role]] in ''Dawn of Justice'', news of which was confirmed in August 2013.<ref name=affleckbatman>{{cite web|url=https://hollywoodreporter.com/news/ben-affleck-is-batman-man-612907|title=Ben Affleck is Batman for 'Man of Steel' Sequel|date=August 22, 2013|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|access-date=October 1, 2014|first=Sophie|last=Schilacci|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911043407/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/ben-affleck-is-batman-man-612907/|archive-date=September 11, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The casting choice was contingent on studio demands for an older Batman to contrast with a younger [[Superman (DC Extended Universe)|Superman]] ([[Henry Cavill]]).<ref name="Abid"/> Filming occurred in 2014, and following multiples changes in the exhibition schedule, Warner Bros. released the film in March 2016.<ref>{{cite web |first=Adam|last=Graham |url=https://www.detroitnews.com/story/entertainment/movies/2016/03/23/batman-superman-puts-detroit-big-screen/82155512/ |title='Batman v Superman' puts Detroit on the big screen |website=[[The Detroit News]] |date=March 23, 2016 | access-date = December 29, 2025 | archive-date = January 26, 2022 | archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20220126082747/https://www.detroitnews.com/story/entertainment/movies/2016/03/23/batman-superman-puts-detroit-big-screen/82155512/ | url-status = live |url-access=subscription}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/news/movienews.php?id=113669 |title=Warner Bros. Pictures Pushes Batman vs. Superman Back to 2016 |work=[[ComingSoon.net]] |date=January 17, 2014 |access-date=January 22, 2014 |archive-date=February 1, 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140201094626/http://www.comingsoon.net/news/movienews.php?id=113669 |url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="March2016Release">{{cite web|url=https://www.thewrap.com/warner-bros-blinks-in-marvel-showdown-batman-v-superman-avoids-captain-america-3/|title=Warner Bros. Blinks in Marvel Showdown: 'Batman v Superman' Avoids 'Captain America 3'|last=Sneider|first=Jeff|work=[[TheWrap]]|date=August 6, 2014|access-date=August 6, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250613072255/https://www.thewrap.com/warner-bros-blinks-in-marvel-showdown-batman-v-superman-avoids-captain-america-3/|archive-date=June 13, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Dawn of Justice'' was derided in professional reviews, while the film fared better with audiences.{{sfn|Brown|2016|p=157}} At the box office, it emerged as the [[2016 in film#Highest-grossing films|seventh highest-grossing film of 2016]] with $874 million.<ref name="BOM">{{cite web |url=https://www.boxofficemojo.com/movies/?id=superman2015.htm |title=Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016) |publisher=[[Box Office Mojo]] |access-date=December 20, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250828010623/https://www.boxofficemojo.com/release/rl2238875137/|archive-date=August 28, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Ensemble roles===
====''Justice League'' (2017)====
{{main|Justice League (film) |l1=''Justice League'' (film)}}

Warner Bros. filed a lawsuit against the estate of [[Joe Shuster]] over the execution of a termination clause barring the disposition of the estate's share of the copyrights to Superman.<ref>{{cite web |first=Brooks |last=Barnes |url=https://archive.nytimes.com/mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/10/17/warner-brothers-wins-legal-case-over-rights-to-superman/ |title=Warner Brothers Wins Legal Case Over Rights to Superman |website=[[The New York Times]] |date=October 17, 2012 | access-date = December 29, 2025 | archive-date = December 29, 2025 | archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20251229231313/https://archive.nytimes.com/mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/10/17/warner-brothers-wins-legal-case-over-rights-to-superman/ | url-status = live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/warner-bros-wins-big-court-379770/|title=Warner Bros. Wins Big Court Ruling in Fight Over Superma|date=October 17, 2012|work=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]|access-date=December 29, 2025|first=Eriq|last=Gardner|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251229231832/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/warner-bros-wins-big-court-379770/|archive-date=December 29, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit|US Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit]] ruled in favor of Warner Bros. in October 2012, and the studio immediately moved forward with plans to create a Justice League film.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Fritz |first=Ben |date=October 29, 2012 |title='Justice League' aims for summer 2015 after Superman victory |work=[[Los Angeles Times]] |url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment/envelope/la-xpm-2012-oct-18-la-et-ct-justice-league-superman-20121018-story.html |url-status=live |access-date=December 29, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131001005624/http://www.slashfilm.com/captain-america-the-winter-soldier-takes-place-two-years-after-the-avengers/ |archive-date=October 1, 2013}}</ref> They hired [[Will Beall]] to conceive the initial draft, which was replaced when Goyer took over as the scriptwriter the following year.<ref>{{cite news|last=Sneider|first=Jeff|url=https://variety.com/2012/film/news/beall-writing-justice-league-for-warner-bros-1118055082/|title=Beall writing 'Justice League' for Warner Bros.|work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|date=June 5, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251027194415/https://variety.com/2012/film/news/beall-writing-justice-league-for-warner-bros-1118055082/|archive-date=October 27, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=September 8, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|last=Finke|first=Nikki|url=https://deadline.com/2013/06/man-of-steel-sequel-underway-with-zack-snyder-and-david-s-goyer-517621/|title='Man Of Steel' Sequel Underway With Zack Snyder And David S. Goyer|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=June 10, 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251025124016/https://deadline.com/2013/06/man-of-steel-sequel-underway-with-zack-snyder-and-david-s-goyer-517621/|archive-date=October 25, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=September 8, 2014}}</ref> Goyer's work was discarded for a rewritten script completed by Terrio in July 2015.<ref>{{cite news|last=Fleming|first=Mike Jr.|url=https://deadline.com/2014/07/comic-con-batman-v-superman-chris-terrio-justice-league-809843/|title='Batman V Superman' Scribe Chris Terrio For 'Justice League'|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=July 25, 2014|access-date=September 8, 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251119002102/https://deadline.com/2014/07/comic-con-batman-v-superman-chris-terrio-justice-league-809843/|archive-date=November 19, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=July 3, 2015 |title=Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice Scenes Described, Justice League Script Complete |publisher=ComingSoon.net |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/movies/news/456329-batman-v-superman-dawn-of-justice-scenes-described-justice-league-script-complete#/slide/1 |url-status=live |access-date=December 29, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150706000559/http://www.comingsoon.net/movies/news/456329-batman-v-superman-dawn-of-justice-scenes-described-justice-league-script-complete#/slide/1 |archive-date=July 6, 2015}}</ref> 

Afterwards, ''Justice League'' fell into a drawn-out development phase involving a succession of rewrites and a dispute concerning the budget, delaying the film's production.<ref name=delay>{{cite web|url=https://www.thewrap.com/justice-league-zack-snyder-batman-v-superman-wonder-woman/|title=How 'Justice League' Became a 'Frankenstein' (Exclusive)|last1=Gonzalez|first1=Umberto|last2=Molloy|first2=Tim|work=[[TheWrap]]|date=November 29, 2017|access-date=December 30, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180720142640/https://www.thewrap.com/justice-league-zack-snyder-batman-v-superman-wonder-woman/|archive-date=July 20, 2018|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Bonomolo |first=Cameron |date=June 11, 2018 |title=Rumor: Geoff Johns' 'Justice League' Rewrites Caused Issues With Chris Terrio, WB Execs |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/06/11/geoff-johns-DC-exit-justice-league-screenwriter-chris-terrio-WB/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717071159/http://comicbook.com/dc/2018/06/11/geoff-johns-DC-exit-justice-league-screenwriter-chris-terrio-WB/ |archive-date=July 17, 2018 |access-date=December 30, 2025 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref><ref name="wsj-11.6.17">{{Cite web |url=https://www.wsj.com/articles/offbeat-super-heroes-take-on-batman-wonder-woman-1509997635 |title=The Quest to Save 'Justice League' |last=Fritz |first=Ben |date=November 6, 2017 |website=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |access-date=December 30, 2025 |archive-date=November 6, 2017 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20171106213714/https://www.wsj.com/articles/offbeat-super-heroes-take-on-batman-wonder-woman-1509997635 |url-status=live }}</ref> Affleck returned as Batman, and Snyder continued his duties as director until his departure due to his daughter's death in 2017.<ref name=DCEU2017>{{Cite news|last1=Child|first1=Ben|title=Five tasks Justice League must complete to save the DC universe|url=https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/nov/01/five-tasks-justice-league-must-complete-to-save-the-dc-universe|access-date=January 1, 2026|newspaper=The Guardian|date=November 1, 2017|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171214124456/https://www.theguardian.com/film/2017/nov/01/five-tasks-justice-league-must-complete-to-save-the-dc-universe|archive-date=December 14, 2017}}</ref><ref name=":5">{{cite web|last=Kit|first=Borys|date=May 22, 2017|title=Zack Snyder Steps Down From 'Justice League' to Deal With Family Tragedy|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/zack-snyder-steps-down-justice-league-deal-family-tragedy-1006455|access-date=August 3, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251014221342/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/zack-snyder-steps-down-justice-league-deal-family-tragedy-1006455/|archive-date=October 14, 2025|url-status=live|website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> His replacement, [[Joss Whedon]], made substantial changes to the script and supervised reshoots, though only Snyder is billed as ''Justice League'' director.<ref name=nytsnydercut>{{Cite web |date=November 19, 2019 |title=Why Ben Affleck and Gal Gadot Are Tweeting #ReleaseTheSnydercut |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/19/movies/snyder-cut-gadot-affleck.html |first=Kyle|last=Buchanan|url-status=live |url-access=limited |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200523063502/https://www.nytimes.com/2019/11/19/movies/snyder-cut-gadot-affleck.html |archive-date=May 23, 2020 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[The New York Times]]}}</ref><ref name="Snyder sole director">{{Cite web |last=Strauss |first=Bob |date=November 15, 2017 |title=Joss Whedon brought 'own flavor' to 'Justice League' after Zack Snyder left |url=https://www.dailynews.com/2017/11/15/joss-whedon-brought-own-flavor-to-justice-league-after-zack-snyder-family-tragedy/ |url-status=live |url-access=subscription |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180627144406/https://www.dailynews.com/2017/11/15/joss-whedon-brought-own-flavor-to-justice-league-after-zack-snyder-family-tragedy/ |archive-date=June 27, 2018 |access-date=December 30, 2025 |website=[[Los Angeles Daily News]]}}</ref> The film was shot from April to October 2016,<ref>{{cite magazine|last=Breznican |first=Anthony |url=https://ew.com/article/2016/02/21/justice-league-starts-april-11/ |title=Justice League begins shooting April 11 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |date=February 21, 2016 |access-date=January 1, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260101181953/https://ew.com/article/2016/02/21/justice-league-starts-april-11/ |archive-date=January 1, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="JLwrap">{{Cite web |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=October 1, 2016 |title=Jason Momoa Thanks 'Justice League' Crew With Shirtless Photo as Filming Wraps (Photo) |url=https://www.thewrap.com/jason-momoa-thanks-justice-league-crew-with-shirtless-photo-as-filming-wraps-photo/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161002062855/http://www.thewrap.com/jason-momoa-thanks-justice-league-crew-with-shirtless-photo-as-filming-wraps-photo/ |archive-date=October 2, 2016 |access-date=January 1, 2026 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref> and was released in November 2017 to largely negative reviews.<ref>{{Cite web|url= https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/justice_league_2017| title=Justice League |publisher=[[Rotten Tomatoes]]|access-date=January 2, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260102030356/https://www.rottentomatoes.com/m/justice_league_2017|archive-date=January 2, 2026|url-status=live}}</ref> It was also a [[box office disappointment]] by failing to recoup enough money to [[break-even]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Sharf |first=Zack |date=November 24, 2017 |title='Justice League' Box Office Bomb: Warner Bros. Could Lose Up to $100 Million on Superhero Tentpole |url=https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/justice-league-box-office-bomb-warner-bros-lose-100-million-1201900710/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250710082324/https://www.indiewire.com/features/general/justice-league-box-office-bomb-warner-bros-lose-100-million-1201900710/ |archive-date=July 10, 2025 |access-date=January 1, 2026 |website=[[IndieWire]]}}</ref> After ''Justice League''{{'s}} release, Whedon was criticized for his treatment of the actors, and Terrio disavowed the film, citing studio interference.<ref name="VFSnyder">{{Cite magazine |last=Breznican |first=Anthony |author-link=Anthony Breznican |date=February 22, 2021 |title=''Justice League'': The Shocking, Exhilarating, Heartbreaking True Story of #TheSnyderCut |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2021/02/the-true-story-of-justice-league-snyder-cut |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251112020300/https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2021/02/the-true-story-of-justice-league-snyder-cut |archive-date=November 12, 2025 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Breznican |first=Anthony |author-link=Anthony Breznican |date=April 8, 2021 |title='Justice League' Screenwriter Chris Terrio Is Super Pissed Off |url=https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2021/04/chris-terrio-justice-league-batman-v-superman |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210409214338/https://www.vanityfair.com/hollywood/2021/04/chris-terrio-justice-league-batman-v-superman |archive-date=April 9, 2021 |access-date=January 1, 2026 |website=[[Vanity Fair (magazine)|Vanity Fair]]}}</ref>

====''Zack Snyder's Justice League'' (2021)====
{{main|Zack Snyder's Justice League |l1=''Zack Snyder's Justice League''}}

Given the negative reaction to ''Justice League'', a fan campaign went viral on social media under the hashtag "#ReleaseTheSnyderCut", calling for the release of Snyder's version of the film.<ref name=nytsnydercut/><ref>{{cite magazine|title=What to Know About the 'Justice League' Snyder Cut—and Why Some People Are Upset About Its Release|url=https://time.com/5839692/snyder-cut-justice-league/|date=May 21, 2020|access-date=August 27, 2020|first=Eliana|last=Dockterman|magazine=[[Time (magazine)|Time]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251118185622/https://time.com/5839692/snyder-cut-justice-league/|archive-date=November 18, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Snyder had an unedited cut of this film version saved on his laptop around the time of his departure, which was presented to Warner Bros. executives in February 2020 in an event he organized with his wife [[Deborah Snyder|Deborah]].<ref name="VFSnyder"/><ref name="hollywoodreporter-5.20.20">{{Cite magazine |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=May 20, 2020 |title="It Will Be an Entirely New Thing": Zack Snyder's $20M-Plus 'Justice League' Cut Plans Revealed |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/justice-league-snyder-cut-plans-revealed-it-will-be-an-new-thing-1295102 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200523145649/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/justice-league-snyder-cut-plans-revealed-it-will-be-an-new-thing-1295102 |archive-date=May 23, 2020 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> That May, it was announced as an official project, a [[director's cut]] titled ''Zack Snyder's Justice League''; the film premiered on [[HBO Max]] in March 2021.<ref>{{cite web|last=Donnelly|first=Matt|date=May 20, 2020|title=Zack Snyder Will Release the 'Snyder Cut' of 'Justice League' on HBO Max|url=https://variety.com/2020/film/news/zack-snyder-release-the-snyder-cut-justice-league-hbo-max-1234611928/|access-date=August 27, 2020|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251115144947/https://variety.com/2020/film/news/zack-snyder-release-the-snyder-cut-justice-league-hbo-max-1234611928/|archive-date=November 15, 2025|url-status=live|language=en}}</ref><ref name="RatedR">{{Cite magazine |last=Hibberd |first=James |date=February 4, 2021 |title=Zack Snyder's Justice League officially gets rated R |url=https://ew.com/movies/justice-league-zack-snyder-r-rating/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210321161257/https://ew.com/movies/justice-league-zack-snyder-r-rating/ |archive-date=March 21, 2021 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> Warner Bros. allocated a $70 million budget to complete work related mostly to visual effects.<ref name="wrap-7.23.20">{{Cite web |last1=Gonzalez |first1=Umberto |last2=Lincoln |first2=Ross A. |date=September 23, 2020 |title='Justice League': Snyder Cut to Include Footage From a Week of Additional Shooting |url=https://www.thewrap.com/justice-league-snyder-additional-shooting/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200926025856/https://www.thewrap.com/justice-league-snyder-additional-shooting/ |archive-date=September 26, 2020 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref> The film does not share continuity with the DCEU.<ref name="Non-canonical">{{Cite web |last=Burwick |first=Kevin |date=July 20, 2020 |title=Zack Snyder's Justice League Is Separate from the DC Cinematic Universe Continuity |url=https://movieweb.com/justice-league-dceu-continuity/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200802231050/https://movieweb.com/justice-league-dceu-continuity/ |archive-date=August 2, 2020 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[MovieWeb]]}}</ref> ''Zack Snyder's Justice League'' features a newly filmed scene with Affleck's Batman.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Sharf |first1=Zack |title=Ben Affleck, Jared Leto Were Never on Set Together to Film the One New 'Justice League' Scene |url=https://www.indiewire.com/2021/03/ben-affleck-jared-leto-justice-league-scene-filmed-separately-1234624531/ |access-date=January 2, 2026 |work=[[IndieWire]] |date=March 18, 2021 |language=en |archive-date=August 10, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220810031008/https://www.indiewire.com/2021/03/ben-affleck-jared-leto-justice-league-scene-filmed-separately-1234624531/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

====Other DCEU films====
