e Flash |url=https://www.vulture.com/2023/08/the-flash-ending-and-george-clooney-cameo-explained.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250818064824/https://www.vulture.com/2023/08/the-flash-ending-and-george-clooney-cameo-explained.html|archive-date=August 18, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=December 4, 2025 |website=[[Vulture (website)|Vulture]] |language=en-us}}</ref> Both actors play alternate versions of DCEU's main continuity Batman (Affleck).<ref name=alternate/> West makes a posthumous cameo appearance in a multiverse sequence developed with a combination of archival footage, [[deepfake]] effects, and [[artificial intelligence]].<ref name="CameosRT">{{Cite web |last=Cremona |first=Patrick |date=June 15, 2023 |title=Meet the cast of ''The Flash'': all the main stars and cameos |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/scifi/the-flash-cast-cameos/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230616035852/https://www.radiotimes.com/movies/scifi/the-flash-cast-cameos/ |archive-date=June 16, 2023 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[Radio Times]]}}</ref><ref name="CameosVariety">{{Cite magazine |last1=Moreau |first1=Jordan |last2=Vary |first2=Adam B. |date=June 16, 2023 |title=''The Flash'' Cameos: All the Batmen and Supermen, Plus That Post-Credits Scene Explained |url=https://variety.com/lists/flash-cameos-ending-post-credits-scene-explained/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230617065803/https://variety.com/lists/flash-cameos-ending-post-credits-scene-explained/ |archive-date=June 17, 2023 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Keaton was set to return to the DCEU in an expanded capacity in ''[[Batgirl (film)|Batgirl]]'' until the film's cancellation in August 2022.<ref name="Keaton">{{Cite web |last1=Kit |first1=Borys |last2=Counch |first2=Aaron |date=December 22, 2021 |title=Michael Keaton Joining 'Batgirl' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/michae