Work on a standalone Batman film was well underway once Warner Bros. cast Affleck in 2014.<ref name="2014Slate">{{Cite magazine |last=Franich |first=Darren |date=October 15, 2014 |title=Warner Bros. announces 10 DC movies, including ''Wonder Woman'' |url=https://ew.com/article/2014/10/15/justice-league-green-lantern-wonder-woman-flash-movies/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170730223226/https://ew.com/article/2014/10/15/justice-league-green-lantern-wonder-woman-flash-movies/ |archive-date=July 30, 2017 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref> He was signed as director, writer, and the film's starring actor, but stepped down amidst various personal and professional struggles.<ref name="AffleckDropReason">{{Cite web |last=Bennett |first=Anita |date=February 18, 2020 |title=Ben Affleck Dropped Out Of ''The Batman'' Amid Fears He'd 'Drink Himself To Death' |url=https://deadline.com/2020/02/ben-affleck-left-the-batman-amid-fears-hed-drink-himself-to-death-1202862905/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200219045758/https://deadline.com/2020/02/ben-affleck-left-the-batman-amid-fears-hed-drink-himself-to-death-1202862905/ |archive-date=February 19, 2020 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Barnes |first1=Brooks |title=Ben Affleck Tried to Drink Away the Pain. Now He's Trying Honesty. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/02/18/movies/ben-affleck.html |access-date=January 2, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=February 18, 2020 |archive-date=February 21, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200221004501/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/02/18/movies/ben-affleck.html |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Matt Reeves]] replaced Affleck as director and writer,<ref name="ReevesDirector">{{Cite web |last=Fleming |first=Mike Jr. |date=February 23, 2017 |title=As You Read Here, Matt Reeves Is New ''Batman'' Director |url=https://deadline.com/2017/02/matt-reeves-is-new-batman-director-1201957224/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170223210543/https://deadline.com/2017/02/matt-reeves-is-new-batman-director-1201957224/ |archive-date=February 23, 2017 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> creating the story anew with [[Mattson Tomlin]] and [[Peter Craig]].<ref name="ReevesNewScript">{{Cite web |last=Hall |first=Jacob |date=March 15, 2017 |title=''The Batman'' Delayed as the Script is Rewritten From Scratch |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/549805/the-batman-screenplay-and-delays/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170315205603/https://www.slashfilm.com/the-batman-screenplay-and-delays/ |archive-date=March 15, 2017 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[SlashFilm|/Film]]}}</ref><ref name="KravitzCast">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=October 14, 2019 |title=''The Batman'' Finds Its Selina Kyle In Zoë Kravitz |url=https://deadline.com/2019/10/the-batman-finds-its-selina-kyle-in-zoe-kravitz-1202759926/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191014210307/https://deadline.com/2019/10/the-batman-finds-its-selina-kyle-in-zoe-kravitz-1202759926/ |archive-date=October 14, 2019 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="VarietyReview">{{Cite magazine |last=Debruge |first=Peter |date=February 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'' Review: A Tortured Robert Pattinson Goes Even Darker Than 'The Dark Knight' |url=https://variety.com/2022/film/reviews/the-batman-review-robert-pattinson-matt-reeves-1235188970/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228170129/https://variety.com/2022/film/reviews/the-batman-review-robert-pattinson-matt-reeves-1235188970/ |archive-date=February 28, 2022 |access-date=March 27, 2022 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Reeves focused on a younger Batman, borrowing from the tradition of a detective story,<ref name="ReevesEarlyCareer">{{Cite magazine |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=June 13, 2018 |title=Warner Bros. Shifts DC Strategy Amid Executive Change-Up |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/joker-batman-suicide-squad-movie-plans-making-sense-dcs-moves-1119489/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180613234324/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/joker-batman-suicide-squad-movie-plans-making-sense-dcs-moves-1119489 |archive-date=June 13, 2018 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="ReevesRework">{{Cite web |last=Topel |first=Fred |date=December 28, 2022 |title=''The Batman'': Read The Screenplay For Matt Reeves' Take On The Caped Crusader |url=https://deadline.com/2022/12/the-batman-script-matt-reeves-peter-craig-screenplay-1235207713/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221230173806/https://deadline.com/2022/12/the-batman-script-matt-reeves-peter-craig-screenplay-1235207713/ |archive-date=December 30, 2022 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="MovieMakerPg1">{{Cite magazine |last=Molloy |first=Tim |date=January 19, 2022 |title=A Detective Story: To Understand Matt Reeves and ''The Batman'', Look to the 1970s {{!}} Page 1 |url=https://www.moviemaker.com/the-batman-matt-reeves-detective-story/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220120061717/https://www.moviemaker.com/the-batman-matt-reeves-detective-story/ |archive-date=January 20, 2022 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[MovieMaker]]}}</ref> and expunged connections to the DCEU in the script.<ref name="TheBatmanSeparate">{{Cite web |last=Liu |first=Narayan |date=August 22, 2020 |title=Pattinson's Batman Confirmed to Exist on a Separate Earth from the Established DCEU |url=https://www.cbr.com/pattinson-batman-confirmed-separate-earth-from-dceu/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200823101324/https://www.cbr.com/pattinson-batman-confirmed-separate-earth-from-dceu/ |archive-date=August 23, 2020 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> To conceptualize the film world, and to further develop the plot, the director sought inspiration from an array of Batman comics and [[New Hollywood]] era films.{{efn|Attributed to multiple sources:<ref name="MovieMakerPg1"/><ref name="EWPattinsonComics">{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=February 18, 2022 |title=''The Batman''{{'s}} Robert Pattinson reveals the unusual comics that inspired his Dark Knight |url=https://ew.com/movies/the-batman-robert-pattinson-comic-book-inspirations/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220218192258/https://ew.com/movies/the-batman-robert-pattinson-comic-book-inspirations/ |archive-date=February 18, 2022 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref><ref name="EsquireComics">{{Cite magazine |last=Davis |first=Johnny |date=February 8, 2022 |title=Director Matt Reeves on the Iconic Comic That Influenced ''The Batman'' |url=https://www.esquire.com/uk/latest-news/a38922356/matt-reeves-the-batman-year-one-inspiration/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220208122240/https://www.esquire.com/uk/latest-news/a38922356/matt-reeves-the-batman-year-one-inspiration/ |archive-date=February 8, 2022 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[Esquire (UK Edition)|Esquire]]}}</ref><ref name="PattinsonReevesNewDetails">{{Cite web |last=Saavedra |first=John |date=February 14, 2022 |title=''The Batman'': Robert Pattinson and Matt Reeves Confirm Exclusive New Details About the Film |url=https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/the-batman-robert-pattinson-matt-reeves-exclusive-new-details-spoilers/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220215035729/https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/the-batman-robert-pattinson-matt-reeves-exclusive-new-details-spoilers/ |archive-date=February 15, 2022 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Den of Geek]]}}</ref><ref name="DoGZeroYear">{{Cite web |last=Saavedra |first=John |date=December 28, 2021 |title=''The Batman'' May Have Confirmed Major Riddler Moment from the Comics |url=https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/the-batman-riddler-zero-year-spoiler/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211228205616/https://www.denofgeek.com/movies/the-batman-riddler-zero-year-spoiler/ |archive-date=December 28, 2021 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Den of Geek]]}}</ref><ref name="ReevesHitchcock">{{Cite web |last=Giroux |first=Jack |date=June 21, 2017 |title=Matt Reeves is Taking a Hitchcock Approach to ''The Batman'' |url=https://www.slashfilm.com/551682/batman-hitchcock-influence/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622003945/https://www.slashfilm.com/batman-hitchcock-influence/ |archive-date=June 22, 2017 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[SlashFilm|/Film]]}}</ref>}} ''The Batman'' universe is separate from the [[DC Universe (franchise)|DC Universe]] (DCU), and hence will exist simultaneously with a DCU Batman within the continuity of a multiverse.<ref name="THREarth2">{{Cite magazine |last1=Couch |first1=Aaron |last2=Kit |first2=Borys |date=April 1, 2021 |title=Ava DuVernay's ''New Gods'', James Wan's ''The Trench'' DC Movies Not Moving Forward at Warner Bros. (Exclusive) |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/ava-duvernays-new-gods-james-wans-the-trench-dc-movies-not-moving-forward-at-warner-bros |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210402191839/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/ava-duvernays-new-gods-james-wans-the-trench-dc-movies-not-moving-forward-at-warner-bros |archive-date=April 2, 2021 |access-date=April 2, 2021 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name=dcubatman>{{Cite news |last1=Barnes |first1=Brooks |title=Managing Movie Superheroes Is About to Get a Lot More Complicated |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/27/business/media/dc-superheroes-movies.html |access-date=January 2, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=December 27, 2020 |archive-date=November 2, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251102213039/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/27/business/media/dc-superheroes-movies.html |url-status=live }}</ref> 

The search for an actor to play Batman was described as "intense", but unusually quick for a superhero film.<ref name="HowPattinsonCast">{{Cite magazine |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=June 4, 2019 |title='Quick' Debates and Secret Screen Tests: How Robert Pattinson Became Batman |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/how-robert-pattinson-became-batman-1215438/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190604223802/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/how-robert-pattinson-became-batman-1215438 |archive-date=June 4, 2019 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Speculation in the media favored [[Robert Pattinson]], and Warner Bros. signed the actor in May 2019, prompting backlash from some fans.<ref name="HowPattinsonCast"/><ref name="PattinsonFrontrunner">{{Cite magazine |last1=Galuppo |first1=Mia |last2=Kit |first2=Borys |date=May 16, 2019 |title=Robert Pattinson Frontrunner to Play Batman in Matt Reeves' DC Movie |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/robert-pattinson-frontrunner-play-batman-1211604/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190517013755/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/robert-pattinson-frontrunner-play-batman-1211604 |archive-date=May 17, 2019 |access-date=January 2, 2026 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref name="r657" >{{cite web | last=Hermanns | first=Grant | title=Robert Pattinson The Batman Casting Backlash Explained By Director | website=[[Screen Rant]] | date=January 26, 2022 | url=https://screenrant.com/batman-movie-robert-pattinson-casting-backlash-director-response/ | access-date=January 2, 2026 | archive-date=March 6, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220306211316/https://screenrant.com/batman-movie-robert-pattinson-casting-backlash-director-response/ | url-status=live }}</ref> Reeves said he wrote the character with Pattinson in mind, having been impressed with his performances in ''[[Good Time (film)|Good Time]]'' (2017) and ''[[High Life (2018 film)|High Life]]'' (2018).<ref name="HowPattinsonCast"/><ref name="k536">{{cite web | last=Sharf | first=Zack | title='The Batman' Guide: 15 Movies and Comics That Inspired Robert Pattinson and Matt Reeves | website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] | date=March 4, 2022| url=https://variety.com/lists/the-batman-movie-inspirations/ | access-date=January 2, 2026 | archive-date=March 6, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220306211316/https://variety.com/lists/the-batman-movie-inspirations/ | url-status=live }}</ref> Pattinson received a $3 million salary for his work.<ref name="PattinsonSalary">{{Cite magazine |last=Donnelly |first=Matt |date=August 18, 2021 |title=From Daniel Craig to Dwayne Johnson, Inside the Biggest Movie Stars' Salaries |url=https://variety.com/2021/film/news/biggest-movie-star-salaries-daniel-craig-dwayne-johnson-1235043305/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210818172418/https://variety.com/2021/film/news/biggest-movie-star-salaries-daniel-craig-dwayne-johnson-1235043305/ |archive-date=August 18, 2021 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Filmmakers spent over a year shooting ''The Batman'' thanks to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]], which halted production for five-and-a-half months.<ref name="ReevesSuspendShotsTone">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=April 9, 2020 |title=''The Batman'' Director Matt Reeves On DC Pic During COVID-19 Hiatus; Unraveling 'Tales From The Loop' & Netflix Slate |url=https://deadline.com/2020/04/the-batman-tales-from-the-loop-netflix-matt-reeves-interview-coronavirus-1202904102/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200412175031/https://deadline.com/2020/04/the-batman-tales-from-the-loop-netflix-matt-reeves-interview-coronavirus-1202904102/ |archive-date=April 12, 2020 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> Postponed twice, Warner Bros. released the film in March 2022.<ref name="Oct2021Date">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=April 20, 2020 |title=''The Batman'' Flies To Fall 2021, ''Sopranos'' Prequel Moves To March & More As Warner Bros. Makes Release Date Changes Due To COVID-19 Climate |url=https://deadline.com/2020/04/the-batman-sopranos-prequel-tom-elvis-presley-movie-warner-bros-release-dates-changes-coronavirus-1202912605/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200420202338/https://deadline.com/2020/04/the-batman-sopranos-prequel-tom-elvis-presley-movie-warner-bros-release-dates-changes-coronavirus-1202912605/ |archive-date=April 20, 2020 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="March2022Date">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=October 5, 2020 |title=''The Batman'' Flies To 2022 Post ''Dune'' Drift, ''Matrix 4'' Moves Up To Christmas 2021, ''Shazam! 2'' Zaps To 2023 & More WB Changes – Update |url=https://deadline.com/2020/10/dune-drifting-away-from-december-to-october-2021-1234591593/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201006124701/https://deadline.com/2020/10/dune-drifting-away-from-december-to-october-2021-1234591593/ |archive-date=October 6, 2020 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>

===''The Batman: Part II'' (2028)===
{{Main|The Batman: Part II |l1=''The Batman: Part II''}}
A sequel, ''The Batman: Part II'', was announced in April 2022; Reeves, Tomlin, and Pattinson will reprise their respective roles.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rubin |first=Rebecca |date=April 26, 2022 |title=Robert Pattinson Returning for ''The Batman'' Sequel |url=https://variety.com/2022/film/news/the-batman-sequel-robert-pattinson-1235241667/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220426234729/https://variety.com/2022/film/news/the-batman-sequel-robert-pattinson-1235241667/ |archive-date=April 26, 2022 |access-date=April 26, 2022 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Parker |first1=Ryan |last2=McClintock |first2=Pamela |date=April 26, 2022 |title='The Batman' Sequel Set With Robert Pattinson and Director Matt Reeves |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/the-batman-sequel-announced-cinemacon-1235135891/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220428031429/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/the-batman-sequel-announced-cinemacon-1235135891/ |archive-date=April 28, 2022 |access-date=April 26, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> The production was delayed to accommodate changes in the writing, and a completed script was submitted in June 2025.<ref name="Part2ScriptComplete">{{Cite web |last=Loving |first=Casey |date=June 27, 2025 |title=Matt Reeves Finally Finishes ''The Batman: Part II'' Script |url=https://www.thewrap.com/matt-reeves-finishes-the-batman-2-script/ |url-access=limited |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250627230149/https://www.thewrap.com/matt-reeves-finishes-the-batman-2-script/ |archive-date=June 27, 2025 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |website=[[TheWrap]]}}</ref><ref name="Part2FilmingReeves">{{Cite magazine |last1=Mendoza |first1=Leia |last2=Malkin |first2=Marc |date=September 14, 2025 |title=Robert Pattinson Read ''The Batman 2'' Script From a 'High-Security' Locked 'Pouch'; ''Penguin'' Season 2 Is 'In Discussions', Matt Reeves Says |url=https://variety.com/2025/film/news/robert-pattinson-batman-2-script-penguin-season-2-1236518305/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250917015907/https://variety.com/2025/film/news/robert-pattinson-batman-2-script-penguin-season-2-1236518305/ |archive-date=September 17, 2025 |access-date=January 3, 2026 |magazine=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> ''Part II'' is slated to be released on February 18, 2028.<ref name="Feb2028Delay">{{Cite web |last=D'Alessandro |first=Anthony |date=July 15, 2026 |title=''The Batman II'' Moves to 2028; J.J. Abrams' ''The Great Beyond'' to 2027 |url=https://deadline.com/2026/07/the-batman-ii-jj-abrams-the-great-beyond-release-date-changes-1236982669/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260715135443/https://deadline.com/2026/07/the-batman-ii-jj-abrams-the-great-beyond-release-date-changes-1236982669/ |archive-date=July 15, 2026 |access-date=July 15, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>

==DC Universe==
{{main|DC Universe (franchise)}}

===''The Brave and the Bold''===

In October 2022, [[Warner Bros. Discovery]] formed [[DC Studios]], with filmmakers [[James Gunn]] and [[Peter Safran]] as its co-chairmen and CEOs, to facilitate development of film and TV adaptations within the context of a new shared universe, the DCU.<ref>{{Cite web |last=|first=|date=October 25, 2025 |title=James Gunn and Peter Safran Named Co-Chairmen and CEOs of DC Studios |url=https://www.wbd.com/james-gunn-and-peter-safran-named-co-chairmen-and-ceos-of-dc-studios |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251116124356/https://www.wbd.com/james-gunn-and-peter-safran-named-co-chairmen-and-ceos-of-dc-studios |archive-date=November 16, 2025 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |publisher=[[Warner Bros. Discovery]]}}</ref><ref name=dcuthr/> A Batman film gleaning comic books by [[Grant Morrison]], titled ''The Brave and the Bold'', was confirmed as one of the DCU projects in active development in January 2023. The story will concentrate on Wayne and his relationship with his teenage son [[Damian Wayne|Damian]].<ref name=dcuthr>{{Cite magazine |last=Kit |first=Borys |date=January 31, 2023 |title=DC Slate Unveiled: New Batman, Supergirl Movies, a Green Lantern TV Show, and More from James Gunn, Peter Safran |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/james-gunn-unveils-dc-slate-batman-superman-1235314176/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230131171111/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-features/james-gunn-unveils-dc-slate-batman-superman-1235314176/ |archive-date=January 31, 2023 |access-date=January 31, 2023 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> Warner Bros. enlisted [[Andy Muschietti]] as the film's director, with his sister [[Barbara Muschietti|Barbara]] set to produce through their production company Double Dream, alongside Gunn and Safran.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Donnelly |first=Matt |date=June 16, 2023 |title=New Batman Film 'Brave and the Bold' Lands 'The Flash' Director Andy Muschietti (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/brave-and-the-bold-andy-muschietti-directing-batman-film-the-flash-1235646262/ |access-date=June 18, 2023 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250928193557/https://variety.com/2023/film/news/brave-and-the-bold-andy-muschietti-directing-batman-film-the-flash-1235646262/|archive-date=September 28, 2025|url-status=live|language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last2=Couch |last1=Borys|first1= Kit|first2= Aaron  |date=June 16, 2023 |title='The Flash' Director Andy Muschietti Tackling New Batman Movie 'The Brave and the Bold' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/batman-the-brave-and-the-bold-director-1235331062/ |access-date=June 18, 2023 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250614024233/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/batman-the-brave-and-the-bold-director-1235331062/|archive-date=June 14, 2025|url-status=live|language=en-US}}</ref>  Work on ''The Brave and the Bold'', according to Gunn, remains underway as of 2026, despite reports claiming the film was delayed by [[Paramount Skydance]]'s [[Acquisition of Warner Bros. Discovery by Paramount Skydance|acquisition of Warner Bros.]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tinoco |first=Armando |date=August 26, 2026 |title=James Gunn Gives DCU Update Amid Paramount-Warner Bros. Merger & Debunks Batman's 'The Brave & The Bold' Report |url=https://deadline.com/2026/08/james-gunn-dcu-update-paramount-warner-bros-merger-batman-1237051222/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260828163321/https://deadline.com/2026/08/james-gunn-dcu-update-paramount-warner-bros-merger-batman-1237051222/ |archive-date=August 28, 2026 |access-date=September 19, 2026 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

==''Joker'' films==
{{main|Joker (2019 film) |l1=''Joker'' (2019 film)|Joker: Folie à Deux |l2=''Joker: Folie à Deux''}}

Beginning in 2019, Warner Bros. distributed two standalone films based on the Joker, directed by [[Todd Phillips]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lang |first=Brent |date=August 20, 2024 |title=Todd Phillips Tells All on Making 'Joker 2': Musical Numbers, Method Acting and Joaquin Phoenix's Broadway Dream That Started It All |url=https://variety.com/2024/film/features/todd-phillips-joker-2-movie-interview-1236111122/ |access-date=January 4, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251128002403/https://variety.com/2024/film/features/todd-phillips-joker-2-movie-interview-1236111122/|archive-date=November 28, 2025|url-status=live|language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Anderton |first=Joe |date=October 5, 2024 |title=Todd Phillips rules out Joker 3 or solo movie for Lady Gaga's Harley Quinn|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/movies/a62517789/joker-3-harley-quinn-movie/ |access-date=January 4, 2026 |website=[[Digital Spy]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250928193557/https://variety.com/2023/film/news/brave-and-the-bold-andy-muschietti-directing-batman-film-the-flash-1235646262/|archive-date=September 28, 2025|url-status=live|language=en-US}}</ref> Both films predate Wayne's transformation into Batman.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/guides/news/1857951-joker-2-batman-bruce-wayne-cameo-folie-a-deux |title=Joker 2: Is Batman or Bruce Wayne in Folie à Deux? |first=Tamal|last=Kundu|work=[[ComingSoon.net]] |date=October 3, 2024 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |archive-date=October 5, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241005024158/https://www.comingsoon.net/guides/news/1857951-joker-2-batman-bruce-wayne-cameo-folie-a-deux |url-status=live}}</ref> ''Joker'' depicts an origin story about a failed comedian's (Phoenix) descent into madness, culminating in the murders of Wayne's parents by a masked rioter.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://people.com/joker-folie-a-deux-ending-explained-batman-8719359|title=Joker: Folie à Deux Ending Explained: What Is the Sequel's Connection to Batman?|last=Smart|first=Jack|work=[[People (magazine)|People]]|access-date=January 4, 2026|date=October 3, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250521201226/https://people.com/joker-folie-a-deux-ending-explained-batman-8719359|archive-date=May 21, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.gq-magazine.co.uk/article/joker-2-two-face-twist|title=What's the point of Joker: Folie à Deux's Two-Face twist?|last=King|first=Jack|work=[[GQ]]|access-date=January 4, 2026|date=October 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250317003329/https://www.gq-magazine.co.uk/article/joker-2-two-face-twist|archive-date=March 17, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> The film portrays Wayne as a young child (played by [[Dante Pereira-Olson]]).<ref name="Davis">{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/2018/10/23/joker-bruce-wayne-cast-dante-pereira-olson/|title='Joker': Dante Pereira-Olson Cast as Young Bruce Wayne|last=Davis|first=Brandon|work=[[ComicBook.com]]|access-date=October 23, 2018|date=October 23, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251202025308/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/joker-bruce-wayne-cast-dante-pereira-olson/|archive-date=December 2, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref>

