Batman has appeared in a variety of animated films since the early 1990s.<ref name=dcanimated>{{Cite web |date=September 29, 2025 |title=How to Watch Batman's Animated Movies in Order |url=https://www.dc.com/blog/2025-09-29/how-to-watch-batman-s-animated-movies-in-order |url-status=live |first=Joshua |last=Lapin-Bertone |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251212065854/https://www.dc.com/blog/2025-09-29/how-to-watch-batman-s-animated-movies-in-order |archive-date=December 12, 2025 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |publisher=[[DC Comics]]}}</ref> His first appearance was in ''[[Batman: Mask of the Phantasm]]'' (1993), voiced by [[Kevin Conroy]].{{sfn|Beck|2005|p=31}} It originated as a [[direct-to-video]] release, following the breakout success of [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]'s TV adaptation of the character, ''[[Batman: The Animated Series]]'', itself influenced by the live-action Burton films.{{sfnm|1a1=Beck|1y=2005|1p=32|2a1=Smith|2y=2013|2p=78|3a1=Solomon|3y=2023|3p=144}} ''Mask of Phantasm'' received notice for its subject matter, animation style, and music.{{sfnm|1a1=Beck|1y=2005|1p=32|2a1=Solomon|2y=2023|2p=144}} Conroy continued voicing the character in various productions up to his death in 2022.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Oxenden |first1=McKenna |title=Kevin Conroy, Who Gave Voice to Batman for 3 Decades, Dies at 66 |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/11/arts/television/kevin-conroy-batman-dead.html |access-date=January 4, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=November 11, 2022 |archive-date=April 9, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250409191127/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/11/arts/television/kevin-conroy-batman-dead.html |url-status=live }}</ref> 

Batman is the titular lead in 39 films and features in another 35 in a supporting capacity, generally as part of the Justice League.<ref name=dcanimated/> Warner Bros. occasionally produces theatrical features, as is the case with ''[[Batman: The Killing Joke (film)|Batman: The Killing Joke]]'' (2016) and films of [[The Lego Movie (franchise)|''The Lego Movie'' franchise]], in which [[Will Arnett]] portrays the character.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Muskus |first1=Jeff |title='Batman: The Killing Joke' Finds Kevin Conroy Back Under the (Animated) Cowl |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/07/31/arts/television/batman-the-killing-joke-kevin-conroy-alan-moore.html |access-date=January 4, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=July 29, 2016 |archive-date=October 25, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251025181729/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/07/31/arts/television/batman-the-killing-joke-kevin-conroy-alan-moore.html |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2019/02/06/lego-movie-2-arnett-explains-batman-superman-superfeud/2781912002/|title=Lego Batman feuds with Superman, falls in love in 'Lego Movie 2': Will Arnett explains why|last=Alexander|first=Bryan|website=[[USA Today]]|language=en-US|access-date=December 1, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251130143326/https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2019/02/06/lego-movie-2-arnett-explains-batman-superman-superfeud/2781912002/|archive-date=November 30, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> Numerous actors have voiced Batman, including [[Jensen Ackles]], [[Michael C. Hall]], [[Roger Craig Smith]], and [[Troy Baker]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Draven |first=Derek |date=August 27, 2021 |title=Every Voice Actor Who Played Batman In The Animated Movies |url=https://screenrant.com/every-voice-actor-played-batman-animated-movies/|url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250726093827/https://screenrant.com/every-voice-actor-played-batman-animated-movies/ |archive-date=July 26, 2025 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |website=[[Screen Rant]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Perrino |first=Matthew |date=August 5, 2023 |title=Every Batman Voice Actor In Chronological Order |url=https://movieweb.com/every-batman-voice-actor-in-chronological-order/|url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250304052107/https://movieweb.com/every-batman-voice-actor-in-chronological-order/ |archive-date=March 4, 2025 |access-date=January 4, 2026 |website=[[MovieWeb]]}}</ref> Further development of animated Batman films is ongoing as of 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Motamayor |first=Rafael |date=June 24, 2026 |title='Batman: Knightfall,' Starring Anson Mount and Michael Mando, Premieres to Thunderous Applause at Annecy |url=https://variety.com/2026/film/global/batman-knightfall-warner-bros-animation-dc-comics-1236789035/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260627042550/https://variety.com/2026/film/global/batman-knightfall-warner-bros-animation-dc-comics-1236789035/ |archive-date=June 27, 2026 |access-date=July 15, 2026 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref>

